.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt RAVEN 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm raven
.Nd RavenBSD administration client
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json | Fl -quiet
.Op Fl -color Ns = Ns Ar auto|always|never
.Op Fl -verbose
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -yes
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the single administration client for RavenBSD services, network, logs, configuration and
diagnosis.
It is a client: it talks to the running servers through their versioned control protocols and
never edits live server state behind their back.
The machine-readable contract, including the NDJSON field rules, is maintained in
.Pa architecture/17-modern-userland.md ;
this page documents the user-visible command line and exit status.
.Pp
Every command has a human mode and, where the command supports it, a JSON mode.
JSON output is NDJSON: one object per line, each object carrying
.Va schema
and
.Va kind .
Errors are written to standard error; standard output never contains an error object.
.Pp
The command set is:
.Bl -tag -width "completion"
.It Cm version
Print the version, schema and target information.
.It Cm help Op Ar command
Show general help or help for one command.
.It Cm completion Ar shell
Print a completion script for
.Ar bash ,
.Ar zsh
or
.Ar fish .
.It Cm status
Show host health;
.Xr raven-status 1 .
.It Cm doctor
Run ordered diagnostics;
.Xr raven-doctor 1 .
.It Cm svc
List, inspect and control services;
.Xr raven-svc 1 .
.It Cm config
Validate and show the TOML configuration;
.Xr raven-config 1 .
.It Cm theme
Preview, set or apply the terminal palette;
.Xr raven-theme 1 .
.It Cm net
Reserved: network control.
.It Cm log
Reserved: log access.
.It Cm pkg
Reserved: package access.
.It Cm user
Reserved: user identities.
.It Cm image
Reserved: image management.
.El
.Pp
Reserved names are part of the namespace.
In this build they exit 1 with the
.Dv EUNAVAILABLE
error code and never print placeholder data.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options are accepted before or after the command word.
.Bl -tag -width "--color=policy"
.It Fl -json
Emit NDJSON, one object per line, with no colour and no column alignment.
.It Fl -quiet
Suppress normal output; errors still go to standard error.
.Fl -json
and
.Fl -quiet
together are a usage error.
.It Fl -verbose
Write extra human diagnostics to standard error; no effect on JSON.
.It Fl -color Ns = Ns Ar policy
Select human colour:
.Ar auto
(the default),
.Ar always
or
.Ar never .
.Dv NO_COLOR
disables automatic colour; an explicit
.Ar always
policy overrides it.
JSON never contains escape codes.
.It Fl -dry-run
Mutating commands print a plan object and change nothing.
.It Fl -yes
Assume yes for a destructive action.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help and exit 0.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl -
End option parsing; every later argument is positional.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
With
.Fl -json
every record is one JSON object with
.Va schema
equal to 1 and a command-specific
.Va kind .
Known-but-absent values are
.Dv null ,
not omitted keys.
Timestamps, when present, are RFC 3339 UTC; sizes are bytes and durations milliseconds unless the
field name says otherwise.
The error object has
.Va kind :
.Dq error
and the fields
.Va code ,
.Va message
and
.Va context .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "2"
.It 0
Success; for a mutating command, the requested state is present.
.It 1
Operational failure, including a recognized but unavailable command.
.It 2
Usage error: unknown flag, missing argument, or
.Fl -json
with
.Fl -quiet .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr raven-status 1 ,
.Xr raven-doctor 1 ,
.Xr raven-svc 1 ,
